The term "bug" is used in a formal sense by entomologists to refer to this group of terrestrial insects.
This term is derived from the ancient science of bedbugs, which are insects that adapt to live as parasites on humans.
Both killer bugs and bed bugs are classical species, residing in the nests or homes of their hosts.
Approximately 400,000 cases of multiple sclerosis have been identified across the United States, making it the leading neurological disease among young adults and middle-aged people.
MS is a disease that affects the central nervous system, which consists of the brain, spinal cord, and optic nerves.
Research has found that women are twice as likely to have MS as men.
