Everyone in this moving transport shuttle is connected to one another, and it is helping the private car-based transportation system.
Science today indicates that this carbon economy has displaced one of the stable conditions essential for life, which had supported human evolution for the past two million years.
In society, everyone uses the transportation system. Yet, strangely, nearly everyone has a complaint about the transportation system.
In developed countries, you occasionally hear complaints about water quality or the falling of bridges.
Why do transportation systems generate such complaints and fail on a daily basis? Are transportation engineers simply incompetent, or is there something inherently flawed about the system itself?
