Some people thought they were right, but many others believe the opposite; that the solar system revolves around Earth, including the Sun (and other stars as well).
It seems reasonable, because the Earth does not feel as if it is moving—does it?
The Amazon is the second longest river and the largest river on Earth. It carries eight times more water than the second largest river.
The Amazon is also the widest river on Earth's surface. In some places, its width reaches six miles.
Twenty percent of the water flowing from the world's rivers into the oceans comes from the Amazon.
The main River Amazons is 6,387 kilometers (3,980 miles) long. It collects water from thousands of smaller rivers.
