Some animals, such as elephants and giraffes, come close to cars and will be clearly seen through standard equipment.
Lions, cheetahs, and hyenas are generally shy, and you'll be able to see them much better through a telescope.
A walking safari (also known as "bush walk," "hiking safari," or "footing") refers to hiking for a few hours or several days.
